1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:04,452
Which terminal does the processing center expect each debit to come through?

2
00:00:04,452 --> 00:00:07,654
It only accepts debits from terminals it already knows.

3
00:00:07,654 --> 00:00:14,892
So the terminal module keeps a registry: for each website and card scheme, one merchant ID and one terminal ID.

4
00:00:14,892 --> 00:00:19,392
Uzcard and Humo payments can use different terminals for the very same website.

5
00:00:19,392 --> 00:00:25,714
A terminal is registered only for a website that exists and accepts that card, and the check fails closed.

6
00:00:25,714 --> 00:00:33,738
The database allows one live terminal per website and card, and a merchant and terminal ID pair is never issued twice.

7
00:00:33,738 --> 00:00:38,369
A terminal can be suspended and resumed, and a revoked one never comes back.

8
00:00:38,369 --> 00:00:42,761
Every change is written to an audit log: who, what, and why.

9
00:00:42,761 --> 00:00:49,297
Before every debit, the payment module asks for the live terminal, and no terminal means no debit.

10
00:00:49,297 --> 00:00:59,547
Admins find any terminal by merchant, website, card scheme, or status, or by part of its merchant or terminal ID, and open it to see its history and act on it.

11
00:00:59,547 --> 00:01:03,714
Next, the card schemes themselves: talking to Uzcard and Humo.

